    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "Conclude that $6$ divides $48$ from the sum looking convenient, with no check that $6$ divides both $18$ and $30$.",
      "B": "From $6$ dividing $48$, conclude that every split of $48$ into two addends has both addends multiples of $6$.",
      "C": "Then $6$ divides $18+30$; but if $6$ divides a total, its addends need not both be multiples of $6$.",
      "D": "Use the same closure when $4$ divides $18$ and $6$ divides $30$, with no shared divisor for both numbers."
